# Vantigo application settings.
# Copy this file to `vantigo.env` and adjust the values.
# Every key here is read by apps/server/internal/config/config.go, which is
# the authoritative reference — field comments there document every default
# and every validation rule.

# --- Application and database ------------------------------------------------
# compose.yaml supplies DATABASE_URL directly (not through this file) so it
# can set a different role per service; do not set it here too. APP_URL is
# the public origin only (scheme + host [+ port]) — no path, no trailing
# slash. Accepted Host header values are derived from it plus loopback
# (localhost, 127.0.0.1, [::1]), so a request carrying any other Host is
# rejected with 400. Loopback stays permitted so the container health check,
# which reaches the app in-process on 127.0.0.1, is never rejected.
#
# The port below must match VANTIGO_PORT in `.env` (the host port compose.yaml
# publishes; both default to 8080). Nothing reconciles the two: host filtering
# compares hosts and ignores the port, so a mismatch raises no error at all —
# the stack still starts and still serves, but every invitation and
# password-reset link it mails points at a port nobody is listening on. Change
# one and you must change the other.
APP_URL=http://localhost:8080
# APP_BASE_PATH=/vantigo

# How long the process drains in-flight work on shutdown before it exits.
# compose.yaml's stop_grace_period on the vantigo service must exceed this,
# or Compose sends SIGKILL before the drain can finish.
# SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT=30s

# --- Transport security ------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS BEFORE EXPOSING THE STACK TO ANYONE.
#
# Transport is yours to choose and the application does not second-guess
# it. This quick-start stack serves http://localhost:8080 and talks to the
# bundled PostgreSQL container over the private compose network with no
# certificate authority anywhere. What that costs you the moment anything
# here is reachable from a network you do not control: session cookies and
# the bearer links in invitation and password-reset mails travel in the
# clear (an http APP_URL also means cookies are set without the Secure
# attribute), and so do the database credentials.
#
# For a real deployment:
#   - put the stack behind a TLS-terminating reverse proxy and set
#     APP_URL=https://vantigo.example.com;
#   - if PostgreSQL is reached across a network, add sslmode=verify-full
#     (or verify-ca) to DATABASE_URL on both services in compose.yaml —
#     see deploy/compose/README.md;
#   - keep SMTP_TLS at "starttls" or "implicit" (see below).
# See docs/transport-security.md.

# Emit the browser content security policy as report-only instead of
# enforcing it. Only needed while diagnosing a customized frontend; it
# disables the protection while set.
# CSP_REPORT_ONLY=1

# --- First-owner bootstrap ----------------------------------------------------
# Required. This stack runs outside development, so the API refuses to start
# without an explicitly configured secret; it is never generated or logged
# for you. Generate a high-entropy value yourself, for example `openssl rand
# -base64 32`, set it below, then visit /setup to create the first Owner
# account. Remove or rotate this secret once the Owner account exists.
BOOTSTRAP_SECRET=

# Process-wide key material (CSRF tokens, cookie signing, and encrypting
# TOTP secrets — the AES-256-GCM key is derived from this via HKDF-SHA256,
# one derived key per purpose). Required, at least 32 bytes. Generate with
# `openssl rand -base64 32` and never rotate it without a migration plan: a
# rotation invalidates every open session and every TOTP secret encrypted
# under the old value.
APP_SECRET=

# Optional: an email that, when it matches a bootstrapped Owner's address
# case-insensitively, also grants that account SystemAdmin.
# SYSTEM_ADMIN_EMAIL=

# --- Identity and authentication ---------------------------------------------
# Outside development, the API refuses to start unless privileged MFA (TOTP
# or a passkey) is required for the Owner and SystemAdmin roles, or this flag
# deliberately accepts running without it. Without MFA, a compromised Owner
# or SystemAdmin password alone is enough to reach every identity and tenant
# control-plane endpoint (https://github.com/vantigo-io/vantigo/issues/15).
# This quick-start stack has nobody around to enroll MFA before it would lock
# the first Owner out, so the flag is set below to let the stack start at
# all. For a real deployment, remove this line, set OWNERS_REQUIRE_MFA=1
# instead, and enroll MFA for the Owner account from /settings right after
# /setup creates it (a session that has not enrolled yet is still permitted
# to reach the MFA setup endpoints, so this is never a lockout).
OWNERS_ALLOW_INSECURE_NO_MFA=1
# OWNERS_REQUIRE_MFA=1
# MFA_ISSUER=Vantigo

# SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT=8h
# SESSION_PRIVILEGED_IDLE_TIMEOUT=2h
# SESSION_ABSOLUTE_LIFETIME=24h
# SESSION_PRIVILEGED_ABSOLUTE_LIFETIME=8h

# INVITATION_LIFETIME=168h
# INVITATION_ACCEPT_URL derives from APP_URL + APP_BASE_PATH by default and
# must contain the literal "{token}" placeholder.
# INVITATION_ACCEPT_URL=https://vantigo.example.com/invitations/accept?token={token}
# PASSWORD_RESET_URL derives from APP_URL + APP_BASE_PATH by default and must
# contain the literal "{email}" and "{token}" placeholders.
# PASSWORD_RESET_URL=https://vantigo.example.com/password-reset?email={email}&token={token}

# Optional static workforce OIDC (one startup-configured provider; restart to
# change). Unset OIDC_PROVIDER is fail-closed (OIDC disabled). Provider is
# exactly "entra" or "google". The callback is fixed at
# /api/v1/identity/oidc/callback.
# OIDC_PROVIDER=entra
# OIDC_AUTHORITY=https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant-guid>/v2.0
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=<guid>
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=<inject-from-secret-store-without-trimming>
# Or workload identity federation instead of a client secret (entra only;
# mutually exclusive with OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET). The token file is read fresh
# for each authorization-code redemption. AZURE_FEDERATED_TOKEN_FILE is used
# when OIDC_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE is unset.
# OIDC_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE=/var/run/secrets/azure/tokens/azure-identity-token
# OIDC_DISPLAY_NAME=Workforce SSO
# For Google, use the exact issuer, a client ID ending in
# .apps.googleusercontent.com, and at least one bare Workspace domain:
# OIDC_PROVIDER=google
# OIDC_AUTHORITY=https://accounts.google.com
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=<client-id>.apps.googleusercontent.com
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=<inject-from-secret-store-without-trimming>
# OIDC_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=example.com,example.org

# --- SCIM provisioning ---------------------------------------------------------
# SCIM uses /api/v1/identity/scim/v2 and a startup-bound bearer token.
# Unset SCIM_TOKEN disables SCIM. Inject the token from a secret store; it
# must not contain whitespace.
# SCIM_TOKEN=<inject-from-secret-store>
# Optional rotation overlap: SCIM_PREVIOUS_TOKEN plus a future RFC 3339
# expiry no more than 24 hours after startup.
# SCIM_PREVIOUS_TOKEN=<inject-from-secret-store>
# SCIM_PREVIOUS_TOKEN_EXPIRES_AT=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z

# --- Application email (identity invitations and password recovery) -----------
# SMTP_HOST and SMTP_FROM below are REQUIRED FOR THE SERVER TO START AT ALL.
# They are not merely required in order to send mail: this stack runs outside
# development, where MAIL_DRIVER defaults to "smtp", and the smtp driver makes
# both of them mandatory. Configuration is loaded before the command runs, so
# leaving either blank fails the `migrate` job exactly as it fails `api` — and
# compose.yaml starts `vantigo` only once `vantigo-migrate` has completed
# successfully, so the whole stack stays down with:
#
#   invalid configuration:
#     SMTP_HOST: is required
#     SMTP_FROM: is required
#
# That is why they ship set rather than commented out: a fresh copy of this
# file boots as it stands. The placeholders are not a working relay, though.
# Until you replace them with one, the stack starts and serves normally but
# delivers no mail at all — which means nobody can be invited and no password
# can be recovered, since both of those flows are mail-delivered bearer links.
# Replace them before the deployment is used by anyone but you.
#
# SMTP_FROM is parsed as a plain address: "no-reply@example.com" is accepted,
# "Vantigo <no-reply@example.com>" is rejected at startup.
#
# MAIL_DRIVER is deliberately left unset, since it already defaults to "smtp"
# here. Do not set it to "log": that driver writes mail contents to the
# container log instead of sending them, and is rejected outside development
# because those mails carry bearer links.
# MAIL_DRIVER=smtp
SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
SMTP_FROM=no-reply@example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USERNAME=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
# "starttls" (default) or "implicit" negotiate TLS; "none" is plaintext — your
# choice, see docs/transport-security.md for what it costs.
# SMTP_TLS=starttls

# --- Business modules -----------------------------------------------------------
# Comma list of business modules this deployment enables. identity is always
# mounted and never listed here. Unset enables every module this binary can
# mount: customers, products, energy, communications (energy and
# communications each require customers). To run a smaller install, list only
# what you want, for example:
# MODULES=customers,products
MODULES=customers,products,energy,communications

# Whether this container also runs every enabled module's background workers
# (outbox delivery, retention, attachment cleanup) in-process alongside
# serving. Default on, for this single-container deployment shape. A
# deployment that scales the API horizontally should set this to 0 on every
# API replica and run one dedicated `worker` container instead (see
# README.md "Background workers").
# WORKERS_IN_PROCESS=0

# --- Customers: Brønnøysundregisteret lookup ------------------------------------
# The customers module's only outbound HTTP dependency, used to look up
# Norwegian organizations. Defaults to the public production API.
# BRREG_BASE_URL=https://data.brreg.no
# BRREG_TIMEOUT=15s

# --- Object storage ---------------------------------------------------------
# Unset (the default) leaves storage unconfigured: the process still starts,
# but every storage operation (Communications attachments) fails with a
# clear "not configured" error instead of the process refusing to boot.
# "fs" is the only supported provider today.
# STORAGE_PROVIDER=fs
# STORAGE_FS_ROOT=/data/vantigo-storage
# Relaxes the fs driver's group/world-writable root check. Only accepted
# when APP_ENV=development; rejected at startup outside it.
# STORAGE_FS_ALLOW_INSECURE_ROOT=1

# --- Communications: attachments and retention ----------------------------------
# COMMUNICATIONS_ATTACHMENT_MAX_BYTES=10485760
# How long a staged attachment stays valid before the retention worker
# sweeps it.
# COMMUNICATIONS_UPLOAD_EXPIRY=24h
# How old terminal communication history must be before the retention
# worker deletes it.
# COMMUNICATIONS_RETENTION_DAYS=365
# COMMUNICATIONS_RETENTION_BATCH_SIZE=100
# How often the retention worker runs a cycle.
# COMMUNICATIONS_RETENTION_POLL=1h
#
# Per-channel SMTP credentials (the mailboxes messages actually send through)
# are configured through the Communications API and sealed at rest with a key
# derived from APP_SECRET, not set as environment variables here.

# --- Communications: AI draft and suggestion features ----------------------------
# Both operations answer 503 ai_unavailable unless all three of these are
# set and the provider is "openai". Off by default.
# COMMUNICATIONS_AI_ENABLED=1
# COMMUNICATIONS_AI_PROVIDER=openai
# COMMUNICATIONS_AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# COMMUNICATIONS_AI_API_KEY=<inject-from-secret-store>

# --- Reverse proxy ------------------------------------------------------------
# When running behind a TLS-terminating reverse proxy, trust exactly that
# proxy so forwarded scheme/host/client-address headers are honored.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1
# TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=10.0.0.0/24

# --- Logging -------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- Branding ------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP_TITLE=Vantigo
# APP_LOGO_URL=/logo.svg
# APP_SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@example.com
# APP_SUPPORT_PHONE=+47 00 00 00 00
# APP_SUPPORT_URL=https://example.com/support

# --- Observability ------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenTelemetry traces, metrics and logs. Off unless an OTLP endpoint is set;
# these are the standard OTel SDK environment variables, read directly by the
# OTLP exporter rather than by config.go.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4317
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=grpc
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=x-api-key=secret
